{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## Investigation 2026-10-31: neither hypothesis fired; the step-4 job ran a real review and produced a real BLOCK\n\nRead-only investigation on `origin/main` `757ca4852d7`. No code changed, ticket not claimed.\n\n### Observation 1 — the stored sidecars for story `6b66-9378-ebb1-446c`\n\nThe step-4 job left its own `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecar (`1793158045669017902-…-REVIEW_RESULT.json`), written between the 13→14 `file_impact` edit (`1793157816…`) and the forced run (`1793158405…`):\n\n- `verdict: BLOCK`, `material_fingerprint: 61a3ad8cb11e3d44` (the **new** material; step 2's was `9ed6f66a440b5341`), `coverage.det.P4.file_impact: 14`, `checkpoint.chunks_resumed: 0 of 14` — a full fresh Pass 1.\n- 4 findings: 1 `block` (`fcf1d7edbaceb08b2`, G1G2, steps.py:230 docstring still says `severity`; impact 1.0 → priority 1.0, threshold 0.8, reason `high-priority+criterion-opted-in`), 2 advisory, 1 dropped.\n\nThe forced run's sidecar (`1793158412475539140-…`) has the same material fingerprint, `chunks_resumed: 14 of 14`, and the **same** finding `fcf1d7edbaceb08b2` rescored to impact 0.55 → priority 0.55 → `default-advisory`. That rescoring is the entire BLOCK→PASS difference between steps 4 and 6.\n\nSo the premise \"returned the previous run's BLOCK with no findings\" does not match the stored record: step 4 produced 4 findings of its own against the 14-path material.\n\n### Observation 2 — where `stale-material` and the old `signed_at` came from\n\n`gate_status` attaches `durable` = `plan_review_status(ticket)`, the ticket's **current attestation currency** (`llm/gate_runs.py` `_durable_verdict`; documented in the d80d design and the `gate_status` docstring as signed-certificate currency). A BLOCK never signs, so after step 4 the only attestation on the ticket was still step 2's, now stale because `file_impact` changed. `durable.verdict: stale-material` with step 2's `signed_at` is that attestation being reported, next to the run's own `verdict: BLOCK`. `status: passed` means the run completed (`_mcp_llm._terminal_from_result`: \"a BLOCK is a run that COMPLETED\"), and `findings.readable: true` correctly pointed at step 4's own sidecar.\n\n### Experiment — seam reproduction (scratch test, not committed)\n\nReal temp store, offline `_CountingFake` runner, spies on `reuse.idempotent_reuse` / `reuse.verdict_reuse`:\n\n1. `file_impact` [a.py] → review → PASS, signed (`plan_review_status`: certified).\n2. `file_impact` → [a.py, b.py]. `plan_review_status` → `stale-material`, \"changed: file_impact (1 -> 2 paths)\", same `signed_at` as step 1.\n3. Non-forced review: `idempotent_reuse` returned `None`, `verdict_reuse` returned `None`, LLM calls 12 → 24 (full re-review).\n4. A completed-BLOCK run record → `gate_run_status` returns `status: passed`, `verdict: BLOCK`, `durable.verdict: stale-material` with the prior attestation — the exact payload shape reported in step 4.\n\nPre-LLM paths checked in code as well: `claimability.not_claimable_verdict` returns only INDETERMINATE; `workflow_ops.plan_review_precheck` returns a BLOCK only with DET blocking findings attached; `drift_refresh` is not force-gated, so it cannot explain a force asymmetry. None produces `stale-material` — only attestation validation does.\n\n### Not established\n\n- Where `plan_reviews: 0` came from. MCP `show_ticket` has no such field; `plan_reviews` is an `audit_trail` field (`audit/read.py`), which lists all `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecars. On the local store it would have shown step 4's sidecar. A lagging MCP-server store view (as in `painted-epidermal-shelduck`) is one untested explanation.\n- The `neon-piratic-dragon` close refusal (15 → 16 paths) followed by an unforced PASS is consistent with correct behaviour: the edit staled the attestation, and the re-review signed a fresh one.\n\nScratch test and log: `.rebar/scratch/s6028/` in worktree `fix-stale-block-reuse`."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793495880726351001,"uuid":"cc4c213b-3da8-46c7-88fe-541a61bdfd34"}